WEBVTT


00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.840
You have a new to you yarn that you'd
like to knit with and where do you start?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:12.330
Now the ball band may gave you some
information about the suggested needles to

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:18.000
use for hand knitting and what stitches
you might get, but as machine knitters,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.350
this doesn't tell us anything.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.150
This doesn't tell us what tension to
turn on the tension dial of your machine.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.930
Let's spend some time today playing with
a get-acquainted swatch . Now when we're

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:37.870
talking about a get-acquainted swatch,
I used to call this a tension swatch, so

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:43.060
it's just a little swatch that lets you
know how the yarn is going to knit up.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.170
The concept of a get acquainted swatch
was introduced to me by a fellow knitter,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.420
Nancy, who knits a lot.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.920
She does production knitting.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:58.080
And anytime she gets a new yarn, she casts
on and starts knitting with that yarn in

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.250
the stitch pattern that she's hoping to
use, and she'll start way down at the

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.080
tightest tension and work all the way up
to the loosest tension, marking as she

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.530
goes.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.620
Not to be confused with the gauge swatch,
a gauge swatch is what you knit so that

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.130
you can

00:01:14.415 --> 00:01:17.054
calculate what your stitches and rows are.

00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:20.505
I'm talking about a get-acquainted swatch.

00:01:20.835 --> 00:01:25.755
It's just a way for you to play around
with the yarn to see how it's going to

00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:27.345
knit on your machine.

00:01:28.185 --> 00:01:34.095
What tension that you like, the feel
of as you're knitting this new yarn.

00:01:35.115 --> 00:01:39.495
I have this new yarn and I don't know what
to do with it, so I'm going to cast on a

00:01:39.495 --> 00:01:40.485
few stitches.

00:01:40.515 --> 00:01:42.675
Yeah, maybe 20 stitches or so.

00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:47.205
Now in my experience, I know that
this is a worsted weight yarn.

00:01:47.235 --> 00:01:48.765
I'm looking at the ball band.

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:54.645
It tells me information that will let me
know that this is probably a bulky or a

00:01:54.645 --> 00:01:55.665
mid gauge yarn.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:01.020
I'll cast on a few stitches
and just start knitting.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:01.679
Now.

00:02:01.679 --> 00:02:06.000
Also, with some experience, I've learned
that you know, this worsted weight yarn is

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.199
going to knit somewhere in about the
middle of my tension dial, so I'm probably

00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:14.790
not going to knit this heavy, heavy
yarn at attention zero, right?

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.859
And tension 10 at the opposite end of
the gauge is probably going to be way too

00:02:19.859 --> 00:02:20.280
loose.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.490
I'll start at about the
middle of the tension dial.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.670
So for my tension swatch or my
get-acquainted swatch, I just cast on

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.150
maybe about 20 stitches or
so and knit for a little bit.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.280
I started at tension 7, sort of middle
of the range of my tension dial.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.830
I'll knit for an inch or so,
and then mark my tension.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.950
I use eyelets to mark the tension

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.460
and then knit a couple more inches.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:57.090
Now immediately as I'm knitting, I can
tell tension 7 with this yarn is just too

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:04.380
loose for me, so I'm going to crank down
the tension by one full number, put in

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.180
some eyelets again, I'll take it
down to 6 and knit for a few inches.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.290
Now that's feeling a lot better.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.040
Just to be on the safe side.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.960
I'm going to crank it down
one more tension to a 5.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:27.520
Again, marking with eyelets, just so I
have some space in between these areas.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.800
And I can tell as it's coming off the
machine that this might be a little bit

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.520
too tight.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.480
I'll just drop this
swatch off the machine.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:49.690
Now again, I can just feel and
get a feel for what I like.

00:03:50.859 --> 00:03:52.070
This is in stockinette.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.830
If I was knitting in a stitch pattern, I
would do it in the stitch pattern as well.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:01.660
And honestly, with this yarn, if I was
going to knit in tuck , I might knit at

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.230
the tension

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:02.850
7.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.660
You just need to play.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.560
We're giving you permission to play with
the yarn and play with your machine.

00:04:11.325 --> 00:04:16.200
Now, another thing that a tension
swatch can do for you is show you what's

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.579
happening with this yarn.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.459
Maybe the yarn will bias.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.500
Maybe the yarn isn't appropriate
for the knitting machine.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:32.190
Um, if you're worrying about the yarn
bleeding or shrinking, it's good to play

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.380
with this swatch and see what happens.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.940
If you throw this in the machine and it
shrinks down, you'll have an idea of what

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.320
tension to knit it at so that you
maintain the feel that you like.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.200
Nancy puts a tag on her, get-acquainted
swatch, and then puts it in with the cone

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.180
or the balls, and if she's going to store
the yarn, so that she has something to

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.480
reference, she puts as much
detail on that tag as she can.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:02.730
So she remembers what machine she used,
what tension she use, what she did to this

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.300
swatch, and, and the brand name and when
she bought it and all that good stuff.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.310
So put as much detail as you can.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:13.650
So when you go back to buy this yarn
again, you have the facts and you can get

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.520
knitting quickly.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:20.609
So now that I have this tension swatch,
I'm going to go ahead and knit my gauge

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:24.419
swatch, measure this gauge swatch.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:30.870
I'll dress it, hang it, do whatever I need
to the proper way for a gauge swatch, and

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.219
I'm ready to get knitting.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.489
My garment will have the proper gauge
and it'll feel the way I want it to feel.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.799
So I'll use a Knit it Now pattern.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.390
I'll draft my own pattern.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:45.750
I'll use software based on my gauge.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.940
I'm not matching anybody else's gauge.

00:05:48.765 --> 00:05:53.085
If you struggle with your knitting and
your knitted items don't come out the

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:53.895
right size.

00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:56.565
Swatching is not optional.

00:05:57.164 --> 00:06:02.205
We have an entire classroom at Knit
it Now on the subject of swatching.

00:06:02.765 --> 00:06:05.974
Knititnow.com/SWATCH.

00:06:06.815 --> 00:06:11.414
I hope you'll embrace knitting of
getting-acquainted swatch when you try new

00:06:11.414 --> 00:06:11.865
yarn.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:19.290
It'll save you time and also open up a
world of possibilities with the wide range

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.320
of yarns that we have available
to use on our knitting machines.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.910
Until next time, thanks for watching.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.170
Happy knitting.

